---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import TaxCalculator from '../islands/TaxCalculator.jsx'
import { SITE_URL } from '../lib/site.js'

const description =
  "Compare the tax on a corpus redeemed after 18 in your child's name with the same corpus in yours. Equity and debt funds, gold, FDs. Free, no signup."
const jsonLd = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Child Investment Tax Calculator',
  url: `${SITE_URL}/tax-calculator/`,
  description,
  applicationCategory: 'FinanceApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any',
  isAccessibleForFree: true,
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'INR' },
  provider: { '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#organization` },
}]
---
<Base
  title="Child Investment Tax Calculator: Your Name vs Theirs | Nuberry"
  description={description}
  ogTitle="Child investment tax calculator: your name vs theirs"
  ogDescription="The tax on a corpus redeemed after 18 in your child's name, next to the same corpus in yours. Live, with your numbers."
  active="calculator"
  ownWaitlist
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Tax calculator', path: '/tax-calculator/' }]}
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Tools</span>
    <h1 class="display">Child investment tax calculator</h1>
    <p class="lede">The tax on a corpus redeemed after your child turns 18, in their name, next to the same corpus in yours. Live, with your numbers.</p>
    <nav class="tool-tabs" aria-label="Calculators">
      <a href="/calculator/">Milestone calculator</a>
      <a href="/tax-calculator/" aria-current="page">Tax calculator</a>
    </nav>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap calc-wrap">
    <TaxCalculator client:load />
    <p class="tc-seo">
      There is no tax saving while your child is a minor. Under Section 99 of the Income-tax Act, 2025 (earlier Section
      64(1A)), any gains taken before 18 are added to the income of the parent who earns more and taxed like that
      parent's own gains, after a ₹1,500 a year exemption per child. The saving comes later: gains taken after 18 are
      your child's own income, so a child with no other income has their own ₹4 lakh basic exemption plus the ₹1.25 lakh
      a year LTCG exemption under Section 198 (earlier 112A). This calculator assumes the whole corpus is redeemed after
      your child turns 18 and shows the difference across asset classes. How clubbing works, with examples:
      <a href="/blog/tax-on-investments-in-childs-name-clubbing/">Tax on investments in your child's name: clubbing explained</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
